                <pb facs="0318" n="200" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg200"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.9311/359: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-10-15T18:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 15,
                                1928—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 15—9:05
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>771. Secretary’s No. 346 of October 12. Considering the situation in China, as
                    reported to you hitherto, and fully realizing the possibility that the regime
                    which had been given such marked evidence of our confidence might be revealed as
                    nothing more than a transitional phase in the political evolution of China, it
                    seems to me that the matter is resolved into a question whether it is the desire
                    of our Government to make such a gesture in order to demonstrate its sympathy
                    and its confidence in regard to the political ideals towards which the people of
                    China are striving.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
